# Dockerfile.scratch — non-functional placeholder
#
# Marks where next-step-runner's sandboxed execution image will be built
# once engine/internal/sandbox and cmd/next-step-runner have real logic
# (post-v1.0, see docs/security-model.md §5 "Known open items"). Container
# technology itself is not yet chosen — this file exists so the intended
# location is visible in the tree from day one, not because a container
# path is confirmed. If the eventual choice is gVisor, seccomp-based
# isolation, or something else non-container, this file is replaced rather
# than adapted.
#
# Do not build this. It is intentionally not a working image definition.

FROM scratch

# Placeholder — no ENTRYPOINT, no COPY. A real sandbox image would need,
# at minimum: the next-step-runner binary (statically linked, matching the
# repo's no-runtime-dependency distribution model), and nothing else —
# scratch is the deliberate starting point precisely because the isolation
# guarantee this package exists to provide depends on the image carrying
# as little attack surface as possible.
